  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FPFK Resilience Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Program will prioritize the thematic areas of:
- Peace and Peace Resilience,
- Gender Resilience, and 
- Environmental Resilience.
-The church as change agent
Expected Change:
- People in vulnerable situations are living with dignity in a sustainable and peaceful environment. 
- They have the capacity to overcome personal, group and systemic threats to their peace, dignity and environment. 
- They have safe spaces and are making decisions and choices for their wellbeing.  
- People in vulnerable situations have livelihood options that are resilient to climate change impacts. 
- They are food secure, have sustainable sources of clean water and are conserving and utilizing natural resources in a sustainable manner.</narrative>
  </description>
